.TH CCOL_ITER_NEXT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_next \- move a unified iterator on to the next element
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

cmap_iterator *ccol_iter_next(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro moves the iterator on to the next element. It calls the _next_fn
callback of the iterator to do this. At the end of the sequence, the macro
destroys the iterator automatically and gives NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable that ccol_iter_declare() declares, or an iterator
     inside ccol_for_each().
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Gives the new value of the iterator. Gives NULL after the last element.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The iterator is destroyed when ccol_iter_next() gives NULL. Do not call
ccol_iter_destroy() on it after that.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_begin (3),
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3),
.BR ccol_iter_destroy (3)
